Local adaptations for the checked Windows x86-64 adapter:
- Invalid instructions return NULL and set ERROR_INVALID_DATA, instead of
  returning a misleading one-byte success without copying the opcode.
- rel32 overflow reports an unrepresentable relocation, rather than extra=0.
- Widened short branches reject destinations outside signed rel32 range.
- Legacy MSVC typedef workarounds apply only to actual old MSVC compilers.
- The unused DetourSetCodeModule wrapper is omitted from this decoder-only
  build; the adapter permanently disables indirect-target dereferences.
- The checked adapter relocates XBEGIN itself, because this source pin copies
  its rel32 abort target as a MOV immediate, and rewrites LOOPcc/JRCXZ, whose
  rel8-only forms the pin cannot widen.

- The x64 EVEX dispatch accepts scalar-double 0F/F2/W1 MOVSD memory
  load/store (10/11), ADDSD (58), MULSD (59), and 0F38/66/W1
  VFMADD132SD/213SD/231SD (99/A9/B9), with P2=08. Memory MOVSD requires
  reserved vvvv=1111. Original EVEX bytes are preserved; the existing ModRM/SIB
  copier and checked RIP-relative relocation handle the payload. The adapter
  rejects all preceding legacy/REX prefixes. Other valid EVEX forms remain
  unsupported; this restriction is not a general legality test.
  References: Intel SDM Vol. 2A, EVEX encoding and compressed displacement;
  Vol. 2C, VFMADD132SD/VFMADD213SD/VFMADD231SD; Intel XED
  datafiles/avx512f/avx512-foundation-isa.xed.txt (VMOVSD, VADDSD, VMULSD).
  https://github.com/intelxed/xed

APX and all other EVEX profiles remain unsupported. This is a bounded decoder
and relocator, not a software probe engine or a complete instruction-effects
classifier.
